
# HG changeset patch
# User Magnus Melin <mkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi>
# Date 1789552538 -7200
# Node ID bf6c1aaf851975eddd389ab6e2c31b11a9b44f08
# Parent  1841d05ea4fcc3663d36fbc5632748ee6823842e
Bug 2069089 - Don't leak one message's cached sender/recipient name into another. r=BenC

FetchAuthor() and FetchRecipients() use their out parameter as input: FetchAuthor
only computes a name if the string is empty (GetDisplayNameInAddressBook leaves
it alone when there is no card), and FetchRecipients appends to it. The result
is then persisted on the header as the sender_name / recipient_names property.

Since bug 2022456 GetCollationKey passes its result string directly to those
functions, and the binary searches in GetIndexForThread, GetInsertIndexHelper
and GetThreadRootIndex reuse one IdKey for every header they probe. So each
probe inherited the previous probe's name and wrote it to the summary file,
making the message list show a completely unrelated sender while the opened
message showed the correct one. Copying such a message preserves the bad
property, so the wrong sender followed it into other folders.

Truncate the out parameter in all three functions, and bump
mail.displayname.version on upgrade so names already cached incorrectly are
discarded.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325352


